## Starting Point: The Template

### Location

`ste/00-template/` (core engine template) or `workflows/00-template/` (workflow template)

**Contents**:
- `test.sh` - Executable test script with comprehensive structure
- `README.md` - Documentation template with all required sections

### When to Use Template

**Always start with the template** for new STEs. It includes:
- Proper script structure and error handling
- All required sections and documentation
- Best practice patterns for API calls, polling, verification
- SQS/DLQ querying patterns with visibility timeout handling
- Test data seeding guidelines

### Copying the Template

```bash
# Create new STE directory
cd ste
cp -r 00-template XX-your-ste-name

# Make test.sh executable
chmod +x XX-your-ste-name/test.sh

# Edit files
cd XX-your-ste-name
# Update test.sh with your test logic
# Update README.md with your scenario details
```

