## Writing README.md

### Required Sections (From Template)

All sections in `00-template/README.md` are REQUIRED. Key highlights:

#### 1. Purpose (REQUIRED)

Clear description of what the eval tests, why it exists, and what makes it unique.

#### 2. Mermaid Diagram (REQUIRED)

**Every eval MUST include a Mermaid diagram** showing the test flow.

Example structure:
```markdown
## Flow Diagram

\`\`\`mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Test as Test Script
    participant Orch as Orchestrator
    participant Worker as Lambda Worker
    participant SQS as SQS Queue
    participant DLQ as Dead Letter Queue
    
    Test->>Orch: POST /api/v1/workflows/:name/jobs
    Orch-->>Test: 201 Created (jobId)
    
    Orch->>SQS: Publish ValidateCustomer
    SQS->>Worker: Poll message
    Worker-->>Worker: Process (FAIL)
    Worker->>SQS: Retry (attempt 1)
    
    # ... more steps
    
    SQS->>DLQ: Move after maxReceiveCount
    Test->>DLQ: Check for message
    DLQ-->>Test: Message found ✅
\`\`\`
```

**See**: `ste/02-dlq-permanent-failure/README.md` for comprehensive Mermaid diagram examples.

#### 3. Expected Timeline (REQUIRED)

Document when events should occur:

```markdown
| Time     | Event                    | Expected State       |
|----------|--------------------------|----------------------|
| `t=0s`   | Job initiated            | Job created          |
| `t=~2s`  | Source steps complete    | Steps completed      |
| `t=~5s`  | Processing steps complete | Steps completed      |
| `t=~8s`  | ACKs received           | Job COMPLETED ✅     |
```

#### 4. SQS/DLQ Querying Guide (NEW, RECOMMENDED)

If your eval involves SQS or DLQ:
- Include visibility timeout patterns
- Document retry logic
- Explain eventual consistency waits

**See**: `00-template/README.md` sections "Advanced Debugging: SQS/DLQ Querying"

#### 5. Test Data Seeding Guide (NEW, RECOMMENDED)

If your eval uses custom seed data:
- Document the seed script location
- Explain what makes the data special
- Provide verification queries

**See**: `00-template/README.md` section "Seeding Test Data"

