## Best Practices Summary

1. **CRITICAL**: Every new STE MUST have dedicated seed data (never reuse other STEs' test data)
   ```bash
   # Always add to 03-isolated-eval-data.sql with your dedicated consumer
   # Update TEST-DATA-REGISTRY.md with your assignment
   ```
2. ✅ **CRITICAL**: Use only existing helper functions from `shared/helpers.sh` (see Pitfall #-1)
   ```bash
   # ✅ Use get_job_status (check helpers.sh for available functions)
   JOB_STATUS=$(get_job_status "${JOB_ID}")
   ```
3. ✅ **CRITICAL**: `externalSystemId` must be a valid UUID (see Pitfall #0)
   ```bash
   "externalSystemId": "e15fae15-fae1-4ae1-ae15-fae15ae15ae1"  # ✅ Good
   "externalSystemId": "test-eval-15-name"                      # ❌ HTTP 400!
   ```
4. ✅ **CRITICAL**: Use dual-ID capture format for `initiate_job` (see Pitfall #1)
   ```bash
   IFS=':' read -r JOB_ID CORRELATION_ID <<< "$(initiate_job "$PAYLOAD")" || exit 1
   validate_job_id "$JOB_ID" || exit 1
   ```
5. ✅ **CRITICAL**: Specify `jobType` explicitly when testing Orders (see Pitfall #8)
   ```bash
   # For batch: "jobType": "batch"
   # For fan-out: "jobType": "default" (or omit)
   ```
6. ✅ **CRITICAL**: Verify test data exists in database before running (see Pitfall #9)
7. ✅ Always start with `00-template/`
8. ✅ Use `set -e` for error propagation
8. ✅ Validate `JOB_ID` format with `validate_job_id`
9. ✅ Check TEST-DATA-REGISTRY.md before choosing consumer IDs
10. ✅ Use `--visibility-timeout 1` for SQS message inspection
11. ✅ Implement retry logic for eventual consistency (3-5 attempts, 2-3s delays)
12. ✅ Search for job-specific DLQ messages (parallel-safe)
13. ✅ Document seed data in TEST-DATA-REGISTRY.md
14. ✅ Include Mermaid diagram in README.md
15. ✅ Test standalone before adding to run-all.sh
16. ✅ Use generous polling timeouts (expected duration + 50% buffer)
17. ✅ Exit with proper summary (`exit_with_summary $PASS_COUNT $FAIL_COUNT`)
18. ✅ Mark as SAFE or DESTRUCTIVE in run-all.sh
19. ✅ For new entities: Check callback.service.ts recognizes your output step
20. ✅ Test with `--max-parallel=N` to tune concurrency (default: 6)
21. ✅ Use `--skip-checks` to skip preflight checks during rapid iteration

