## Quick Start Workflow

```bash
# 1. Choose next available eval number AND consumer number
# Check ste/ directory and workflows/order-processing/ste/TEST-DATA-REGISTRY.md
# CRITICAL: Always assign a dedicated consumer (e.g., 1033+ range)

# 2. Copy template
cd ste
cp -r 00-template 15-your-eval-name
cd 15-your-eval-name

# 3. Create dedicated seed data (ALWAYS REQUIRED for new evals)
# Add to: workflows/order-processing/source-db/init-scripts/03-isolated-eval-data.sql
# Pattern: Consumer 10XX, Membership 141000XXXX
# Update TEST-DATA-REGISTRY.md with new assignment
# Apply: docker exec dtm-order-processing-source-db psql -U order_user -d order_processing_db -f /docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/03-isolated-eval-data.sql

# 4. Update test.sh
# - Change EVAL_NAME, EVAL_PURPOSE
# - Use YOUR dedicated consumer (from step 1)
# - Implement test logic
# - Add verification checks

# 5. Update README.md
# - Fill in all sections from template
# - Add Mermaid diagram
# - Reference your dedicated seed data
# - Document expected timeline
# - Add troubleshooting tips

# 6. Test standalone
chmod +x test.sh
./test.sh

# 💡 TIP: Check results in ste/.results/parallel/<latest-timestamp>/
# 💡 TIP: Ensure workers are running in Poller mode with count >= 5 for debugging

# 7. Register in run-all.sh
# Add to ALL_EVALS and SAFE_EVALS (or DESTRUCTIVE_EVALS)

# 8. Test in parallel
cd ..
./run-all.sh --eval 15

# 9. Commit and document
git add .
git commit -m "feat(ste): add STE 15 - your-eval-name"
```

